<component name="ProjectRunConfigurationManager">
  <!--
    The Stop-button-doesn't-work complaint only ever applied to "SFL all services": that one runs as
    a Shell Script in a real terminal so it can sequence infra -> build -> tests -> three services
    with readable Maven output, and IntelliJ regularly loses track of the three java processes it
    backgrounds as a result (see scripts/dev/stop-all.sh for the full story). The three Spring Boot
    configs below it were never affected - IntelliJ launches those directly as its own child
    processes, so their Stop buttons are always reliable.

    This compound exists for "I want all three up, launched as real IntelliJ child processes, each
    independently stoppable" - one click starts IFIMP + SSEMP + FTLMP together, each keeps its own
    console tab and its own working Stop button, and each already brings its own database up first
    via its "SFL infrastructure" before-launch step (added on each of the three individually), so
    there's nothing left for the compound itself to sequence.

    It does not build, run tests, or verify a green build first the way "SFL all services" does -
    for that, or for running everything from a real shell, "SFL all services" is still there
    unchanged and is exactly what running "in shell" means: pick whichever suits what you're doing
    right now, both work.
  -->
  <configuration folderName="SFL" name="SFL all services (compound)" type="CompoundRunConfigurationType">
    <toRun name="IFIMP facilities 8091" type="SpringBootApplicationConfigurationType" />
    <toRun name="SSEMP safety security 8092" type="SpringBootApplicationConfigurationType" />
    <toRun name="FTLMP fleet logistics 8093" type="SpringBootApplicationConfigurationType" />
    <method v="2" />
  </configuration>
</component>
